records":"Albuquerque has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"Albuquerque's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 63\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>63\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 59\u00b0F, and the record is 72\u00b0F (1995). The low of <strong>38\u00b0F</strong> was the 25th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 135 since 1892.","t_rec":"Albuquerque has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If Albuquerque's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Albuquerque has set <strong class=\"sig\">7 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 73 that chance alone would give, and <strong>110 record highs</strong>, far more than the 73 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (67). Albuquerque's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on June 26, 1994.","t_chg":"Albuquerque's days and nights both warmed. Nights warmed faster.","p_chg":"Across 133 complete years: Albuquerque's average low has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.48\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.40 to +0.56), about +6.3\u00b0F since 1893. Albuquerque's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.15\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.09 to +0.21), about +2.0\u00b0F since 1893.","t_mon":"Lows rose in all 12 months. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Albuquerque's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.04 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 8.8 inches a year. The wettest year was 1941 (15.88 in); the driest, 1917 (3.29 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 20 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}